; A compound that holds a comparison next to an identifier is an expression,
; so the unknown identifier is an error, not a silent pattern.

2024/01/10 Bookshop
    Expenses:Books                $25.00
    Assets:Cash

test reg 'amount>= 20 and Books' -> 1
__ERROR__
While evaluating value expression:
  ((amount >= 20) & Books)
                    ^^^^^
While handling posting from "$FILE", line 5:
>     Expenses:Books                $25.00
Error: Unknown identifier 'Books'
end test

test reg 'amount>20 and Books' -> 1
__ERROR__
While evaluating value expression:
  ((amount > 20) & Books)
                   ^^^^^
While handling posting from "$FILE", line 5:
>     Expenses:Books                $25.00
Error: Unknown identifier 'Books'
end test
